I’m going to try a more structural correction at the first ReLU layer: compute the exact first-layer ReLU covariance from the known Gaussian preactivation covariance, then affine-match the probe activations to that covariance. This may improve downstream correlations, but it costs extra matrix work, so the evaluator will decide whether it is worth it.
